  "visual_findings": {
    "blocking_issues": [],
    "complete_page_flow": "Title, introduction, four figures, all sections, links, helpfulness/contact widgets and footer are covered by contiguous full-width tiles. Tile edges divide the capture, not the actual layout.",
    "desktop_readability": "The three-pane context image provides orientation at 698.406 CSS px. Small internal text is supplemented by the sharp 471 CSS px profile and 698.406 CSS px editor closeups. Retained Assign to me control remains legible at its native 265 CSS px. No controls are clipped.",
    "mobile_readability": "The native list, profile and conversation views fit the article at about 315.99 CSS px. Names, profile fields, received history, internal note, empty WhatsApp editor and toolbar remain readable. Natural name/message ellipses belong to the app.",
    "presentation": "Full-column lavender stages, white padded frames and rounded borders are consistent. No visible figure captions, figure hyperlinks, extraneous neighboring panel line, Impersonate control, tooltip or horizontal Help-page overflow.",
    "prose_and_accessibility": "Visible prose and alt text correctly distinguish desktop three panels from separate mobile views and an empty WhatsApp editor. Existing qualified ownership/reopening text and links remain present. Figure captions make no send or assignment outcome claim."
  },
  "nonblocking_limits": [
    "Some fictional user-created labels and older conversation previews remain Spanish (for example Prioridad and messages for Emma and Isabella); English interface labels and the focal conversation are translated. These are retained data, not fabricated translations.",
    "The app retains genuine initials avatars and its native notification notice. This review does not claim photo-avatar support or changed browser permissions.",
    "The received WhatsApp example is a disconnected fictional window; the empty editor demonstrates native controls, not registration, delivery, a configured channel selector or a successful send. No seen/cursor outcome is claimed.",
    "Source comparison is scoped to visible renderer/JS/CSS/locales. Runtime 6dc36367 and comparison master 9b59f5ce are distinct; no deployment proof or global test/production parity is implied.",
    "Published filter articles and assets are unchanged and were not newly reviewed here. Search-result coverage and filter legibility remain unresolved.",
    "PNG viewing can be downscaled by the image tool; separate figure captures were inspected alongside actual CSS geometry. No claim of inspecting every source pixel at 1:1 is made."
